\title{penalties7: Penalties as Objects with Exact Derivatives}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Penalties for regularized and Bayesian regression as 'S7' objects: a linear map, a scalar function and hyperparameters, with the value, the exact derivatives in the coefficients and in the hyperparameters, the mixed block, and, for quadratic penalties, the rank, the null space and the log pseudo-determinant that a marginal likelihood criterion consumes. Normalizing constants are kept, so a proper penalty is exactly the negative log-density of its prior. Part of the 'statmodels7' toolkit.
